WEBVTT

NOTE English translation of the spoken Hinglish, not a verbatim transcript. Cue timing is automatically aligned and is not human-verified; it can still be wrong.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.260
Hi everyone! Batch 1 covers the basics of Travelling
Allowance, or TA,

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.300
in simple Hinglish.

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.880
TA concerns travel costs for official duty; it is not

4
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.780
payment for every personal trip.

5
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:18.040
Suppose a Delhi employee goes to Jaipur for an office
inspection:

6
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.240
check TA under the rules for the approved trip.

7
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.220
But if the same employee takes a weekend trip with family,

8
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.720
that is not an official tour.

9
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.120
Another important point: TA and LTC are not the same.

10
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.040
The Department of Expenditure issues Central civilian TA
orders;

11
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.620
check DoPT guidelines for LTC and service rules too.

12
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.380
For example, official training travel and a home-town holiday
claim

13
00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.480
are two different cases.

14
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.740
Railways and the Armed Forces may have separate orders, so
check

15
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.280
the rules for your service.

16
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:55.520
Now the dates. The main TA order was issued on 13 July 2017,

17
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.680
but the changes took effect from 1 July 2017.

18
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.920
For a trip completed on 30 June, check the old rules; for a 2
July

19
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.260
trip, start with the new rules.

20
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.240
The issue date and effective date are not the same.

21
00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.410
Now check protection of old entitlements. If the new order
reduces

22
00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:19.730
a person's or group's existing travel class or mode, the
saving clause

23
00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:24.050
continues the earlier, higher entitlement until, in the normal
course,

24
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.970
a higher entitlement becomes available.

25
00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:30.830
For example, if an officer's earlier approved class was better
than the new table,

26
00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.770
ask the office to check the saving clause and earlier proof.

27
00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:36.830
This does not mean an automatic upgrade for every employee.

28
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.480
TA entitlement depends on Pay Level; Pay Level and the pay

29
00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.240
amount are not the same thing.

30
00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:47.240
In the 2017 order, Pay in the Level means basic pay in the
matrix level;

31
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.800
NPA, MSP or special pay are not added to that definition.

32
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.160
Suppose basic pay is Rs 50,000 and NPA is Rs 10,000:

33
00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.400
under this definition, pay is Rs 50,000, not Rs 60,000.

34
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:04.150
Another example: a Level 7 employee checks travel class

35
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.570
in the Level 6 to 11 row.

36
00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:09.010
But each TA component may be calculated differently.

37
00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:12.810
Do not decide the transfer-grant amount from the travel-class
table alone;

38
00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.130
check that component's separate conditions.

39
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.940
For domestic official tour or training, the travel class

40
00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.840
is determined by Pay Level.

41
00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:26.060
Level 14 and above: business/club air or AC First by train;

42
00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.980
Levels 12 and 13: economy air or AC First.

43
00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:34.760
For example, Level 13A receives Level 13 treatment for TA and
Daily Allowance;

44
00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.480
the letter A alone does not confer business class.

45
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.200
Trip approval and booking rules also matter.

46
00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.370
Levels 6 to 11: economy air or AC Second by train; Level 5 and

47
00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:50.250
below: First Class, AC Third or AC Chair Car by train.

48
00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:54.710
For example, a Level 7 employee on an approved official tour

49
00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.270
may be entitled to an economy flight.

50
00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:59.850
But ordinary LTC does not give Levels 6 to 8 the same air
entitlement;

51
00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:03.370
some special LTC schemes may differ.

52
00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.430
Do not mix tour rules with LTC.

53
00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.660
There is a separate table for some premium trains, including
Rajdhani, Shatabdi,

54
00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.340
Duronto, Premium, Premium Tatkal and Suvidha.

55
00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:19.420
Level 12 and above: Executive or AC First; Levels 6 to 11: AC
Second

56
00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:23.060
or Shatabdi Chair Car; Level 5 and below: AC Third or

57
00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.400
Chair Car, subject to the table.

58
00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.890
For example, a Level 7 employee checks Shatabdi Chair Car
entitlement,

59
00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:32.010
rather than assuming Executive class.

60
00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:36.610
For Premium Tatkal charges and Shatabdi, Rajdhani and Duronto
dynamic or flexi

61
00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:41.190
fares, check the order's exact wording; fixed-fare Tatkal Seva
charges also

62
00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:45.810
continue. For example, when claiming an eligible Shatabdi
dynamic fare,

63
00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.220
check the order's conditions.

64
00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:52.170
Now the 2023 train update. Tejas and Vande Bharat follow

65
00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:55.490
Shatabdi entitlement; Humsafar follows Rajdhani.

66
00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:58.670
Check this mapping for the listed tour, training, transfer

67
00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.310
and retirement journeys.

68
00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:04.230
For example, on an approved Vande Bharat tour, a Level 7
employee checks

69
00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:08.410
Shatabdi Chair Car; for Humsafar, check the Rajdhani class.

70
00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:11.350
A train's name is not an automatic pass to Executive class.

71
00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:16.400
Where two places are not connected by rail, employees entitled
to AC Second

72
00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.540
or higher by train may use an AC bus; others check Deluxe or

73
00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.040
ordinary bus entitlement.

74
00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:26.440
For example, a Level 7 employee must visit a place with no
rail connection;

75
00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:29.760
subject to the other conditions, they may check AC bus
entitlement.

76
00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.600
This is not the complete taxi or road-mileage table.

77
00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:37.030
If both places are connected by rail, public road transport is
allowed,

78
00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:40.410
but the total fare must not exceed the entitled train fare.

79
00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:44.190
For example, if the bus fare is Rs 900 and the entitled train
fare is Rs 1,000,

80
00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:48.190
that fare condition is met; the other checks still apply.

81
00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:51.910
Suppose a Level 7 AC Second seat is unavailable: under this
rule,

82
00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:55.470
a lower class may be used; there is no automatic higher-class
upgrade.

83
00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:00.160
For a Government-account air ticket, this order identifies
three approved

84
00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:05.380
agents: Balmer Lawrie, Ashok Travels and Tours, and IRCTC.

85
00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:10.220
For example, a Level 7 employee may be eligible for air
travel, but

86
00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.680
ticket booking and tour approval must also be checked.

87
00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:17.290
Check the Best Available Fare in the entitled class and fixed
three-hour slot;

88
00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:21.530
also check the order's 10% price band for convenience.

89
00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:24.810
For example, a 10 a.m. flight falls in the 9 a.m. to noon
slot,

90
00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:27.070
not a rolling window.

91
00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:31.250
This is an air-ticket rule; do not apply it automatically to
every rail ticket.

92
00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.530
The guide explains limited relaxation in unavoidable cases.

93
00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:39.360
Booking flights 21 days ahead for tour and LTC is encouraged;

94
00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.800
do not treat it as a mandatory deadline in every case.

95
00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:45.760
If a tour booking is made less than 72 hours before departure,

96
00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.700
the employee must give a reason.

97
00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:51.160
For example, for an urgent tour ticket booked two days before
departure,

98
00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.900
keep a self-declared justification ready.

99
00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:56.240
After the journey, within 72 hours submit the required

100
00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.320
journey-completion certificate; this differs from the booking
justification.

101
00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:03.160
Government-account air travel should not generate mileage
points.

102
00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:08.580
A TA claim for tour, transfer or training normally must be
submitted

103
00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:12.660
within 60 days after the journey; a late claim may be
forfeited,

104
00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:14.640
meaning lost.

105
00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.880
For example, if the journey ends on 1 October 2026, then

106
00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:22.560
2 October is day one and 30 November is day 60.

107
00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.420
Submit on time to the correct office and keep proof.

108
00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:29.260
For retirement TA, the 2021 order set a limit of 180 days

109
00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:33.800
after the journey; tour, transfer and training remain at 60
days.

110
00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:38.100
For example, if an eligible retirement journey ends on 1
October 2026,

111
00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:41.740
day 180 is 30 March 2027.

112
00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:46.440
Remember: the period allowed to make a journey and the
claim-filing deadline

113
00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:50.660
are different. The guide discusses possible review of old
unsettled cases.

114
00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:55.600
If an employee and family travel separately on transfer,

115
00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.000
the claim clock starts separately for each journey.

116
00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:02.660
For example, the employee arrives on 1 October and the family
on 11 October;

117
00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:05.280
their completion dates are counted separately.

118
00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.660
For personal effects or conveyance, separately check the
actual delivery

119
00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.400
date at the new station.

120
00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.970
When a claim is considered submitted also depends on whether

121
00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:17.230
you are your own controlling officer.

122
00:07:17.230 --> 00:07:21.290
If not, check the submission date to the Head of Office or
controlling officer;

123
00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:24.810
if you are your own controlling officer, check the
presentation date

124
00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.390
at the Treasury or Cash Section.

125
00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:30.570
For example, you submit to your controlling officer on day 45,

126
00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:34.090
and Treasury receives it later: subject to the order's
conditions,

127
00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.650
the earlier submission date may matter.

128
00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:37.850
Keep the receipt or acknowledgement safe.

129
00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:43.500
Quick official update: what if a boarding pass is missing? The
2020 DoE

130
00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:47.360
order applies to official tour journeys by Central Government
employees.

131
00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:51.560
If neither a physical nor a digital copy is available, the
prescribed declaration

132
00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:53.380
may be submitted with the TA bill.

133
00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:58.610
For example, a Level 9 employee loses the pass and declares
the actual journey,

134
00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:02.150
PNR details and that the claim is not duplicated.

135
00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:05.170
Employees at Level 10 and below must have the declaration

136
00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.820
countersigned by the controlling officer.

137
00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:11.710
This missing-pass declaration differs from the
journey-completion certificate. The June

138
00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:15.250
2022 order requires the completion certificate within 72

139
00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:19.480
hours of the journey; the TA bill is submitted later under
separate rules.

140
00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:23.950
For example, an employee sends the completion certificate
after a flight. If the

141
00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:27.830
boarding pass is missing, they attach the separate prescribed
declaration to the bill.

142
00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:31.190
A false declaration may lead to disciplinary action and
recovery.

143
00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:36.080
Reimbursement of local travel on official tour depends on
actual expenses

144
00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.800
and the other conditions.

145
00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:42.640
The 2020 DoE clarification removed the city-travel voucher
condition for

146
00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:46.420
Pay Levels 9 to 11, but the self-certification must include
the travel

147
00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.200
period, vehicle number and other details.

148
00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:54.150
For example, a Level 10 employee takes a cab for official
visits. If there is no

149
00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:58.350
receipt, they self-certify the correct expense and vehicle
number; applicable

150
00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.760
limits and other checks still apply.

151
00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:05.130
Even with free boarding and lodging, genuinely incurred local
tour

152
00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:08.230
travel may be claimed under the applicable rules.

153
00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:12.510
For example, a trainee receives free hotel and meals but pays
an eligible

154
00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:16.760
official local-trip expense, which they check against the
rules and evidence.

155
00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:22.150
This Level 9 to 11 voucher relaxation does not automatically
apply to every hotel,

156
00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:24.710
food, transfer or LTC claim.

157
00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:30.520
Now some important differences from DoPT's 1 July 2025 LTC
FAQ.

158
00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:34.640
Eligible family members may travel separately.

159
00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:38.880
If only the family is travelling on LTC, the employee need not
take leave

160
00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:40.240
just for that reason.

161
00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:44.610
For example, the employee works in the office while an
eligible family member

162
00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:46.730
goes on approved LTC.

163
00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:51.090
But when the employee takes LTC, admissible leave is needed; a
weekend

164
00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:55.330
or holiday alone is not enough. This is not an official-tour
TA rule.

165
00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:00.570
The DoPT FAQ says LTC does not cover incidental or
local-journey expenses;

166
00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:04.570
a local taxi from home to the airport is not covered under LTC
either.

167
00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:08.510
For example, do not add the cab from home to the airport for a
family holiday

168
00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:09.780
to that LTC claim.

169
00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:13.410
Official-tour local travel may have different conditions;

170
00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:15.110
do not mix the two systems.

171
00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:21.720
According to the 2025 DoPT FAQ, Tejas, Vande Bharat and
Humsafar

172
00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:25.020
are allowed for LTC according to entitlement.

173
00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:29.860
For example, check the entitled LTC class first; do not assume
Executive

174
00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:32.700
class just because of the train name.

175
00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:37.640
Booking a flight 21 days ahead is encouraged; the FAQ does not
make it

176
00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:40.180
an automatic-forfeiture deadline in every case.

177
00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:44.580
For LTC, the FAQ provides a registration route if there is no
official email:

178
00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:48.340
the office sends the details to an authorized agent.

179
00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:52.920
For example, the office sends the employee's required details
and private email

180
00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:57.760
to the agent. This answer is for LTC; check tour rules
separately.

181
00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:02.540
The FAQ also says the old LTC-80 fare scheme no longer exists.

182
00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:06.240
Check the validity of any special relaxation before booking.

183
00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:10.740
Important correction: the three-agent requirement is not
identical

184
00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:15.500
for every LTC air ticket. DoPT's 2023 instruction is also

185
00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:17.860
included in the 2025 guidelines.

186
00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:22.380
An employee who is not air-entitled on ordinary LTC, but
chooses

187
00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:26.820
to fly without a special dispensation, is not required

188
00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.430
to buy the ticket through only the three agents.

189
00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:33.160
For example, a Level 7 employee chooses to fly on ordinary
LTC;

190
00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.980
check this specific exception.

191
00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:39.190
Reimbursement is limited to the actual airfare or the entitled
train or bus fare

192
00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:41.630
by the shortest route, whichever is less.

193
00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:45.450
For example, the flight costs Rs 8,000 and the eligible rail
fare is Rs 5,000,

194
00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:49.730
so check the Rs 5,000 ceiling and other conditions separately.

195
00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:53.530
For non-air-entitled travel under a valid special
dispensation, authorised

196
00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:57.410
agents have a separate requirement. First verify current
scheme validity

197
00:11:57.410 --> 00:11:59.130
and cancellation rules.

198
00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:05.240
The LTC claim clock differs from official-tour TA. The DoPT
FAQ says

199
00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:09.580
if an advance was drawn, claim within one month after the
return journey.

200
00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:14.180
If no advance was drawn, claim within three months after the
return journey.

201
00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:18.940
For example, an employee without an advance records the return
date and submits

202
00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:21.800
the LTC bill within three months. Do not confuse this with

203
00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.740
the 60-day tour-TA clock.

204
00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:28.550
A late LTC claim is not automatically approved. The FAQ
provides limited

205
00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:32.310
relaxation by the department with Financial Adviser
concurrence.

206
00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:36.210
The stated limits are up to six months without an advance and
three

207
00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:40.150
months with an advance. Where an advance was drawn, the whole
advance

208
00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:43.010
and prescribed penal interest must also be refunded as
required.

209
00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:47.230
For example, a late claimant supplies reasons and documents
and asks the

210
00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:51.410
competent authority for a decision; extra time is not an
automatic right.

211
00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:56.160
For technical resignation, see DoPT's 2022 consolidated order.

212
00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:00.620
If an employee applies through the proper channel for a
Government post, is selected

213
00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:04.700
and must resign for administrative reasons, under the stated
conditions

214
00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:06.280
it may be treated as technical.

215
00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:10.360
For example, an employee is selected for another Government
post through

216
00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:14.940
the approved channel and resigns as required. Past service or
other benefits

217
00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.960
depend on the conditions of separate rules.

218
00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.460
Calling every resignation technical does not make benefits
automatic.

219
00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:24.950
In paragraph 3.6.3 of the same order, appointment through open
competition or

220
00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:27.490
interview to a Central Government post is subject to

221
00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.530
a specific transfer-TA rule.

222
00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:32.790
In that case, a temporary Central Government employee with
regular continuous

223
00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:37.390
service of under three years is not entitled to transfer TA.
For permanent or

224
00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:40.710
provisionally permanent State employees, check the paragraph's
separate wording.

225
00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:44.860
For example, a temporary Central employee with two years of
such service

226
00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:48.340
falls within that stated exclusion. For other cases, check the
appointment

227
00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.000
and service status.

228
00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:54.720
For retirement Composite Transfer Grant, or CTG, DoE's 6
January

229
00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.740
2022 amendment is important.

230
00:13:57.740 --> 00:14:01.800
For retirement settlement, the 20-kilometre condition was
removed,

231
00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:06.620
but an actual change of residence and prescribed declaration
are required. The general

232
00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:09.520
rate is 80% of last month's basic pay, subject to the other

233
00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:10.960
applicable conditions.

234
00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:15.540
For example, with last basic pay of Rs 50,000, eligible full
CTG

235
00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:19.090
is Rs 40,000. The order is effective from its issue date.

236
00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:23.140
For qualifying settlement to or from Andaman and Nicobar or
Lakshadweep

237
00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:26.960
island territories, the order sets CTG at 100% of last basic
pay,

238
00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.020
subject to its terms.

239
00:14:29.020 --> 00:14:32.940
For example, for an eligible island case with Rs 50,000 basic
pay,

240
00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:34.680
check Rs 50,000 at that rate.

241
00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:38.060
The rule to submit a retirement TA claim normally within 180
days

242
00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:41.660
after the journey differs from the period allowed to undertake
the move.

243
00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:47.320
If a TA claim has been kept in abeyance, or pending, for over
a year, the Head of

244
00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:50.000
Department should investigate it.

245
00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:55.040
For example, provide tickets, papers and the reason for delay;
the department

246
00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:59.860
checks genuineness, valid reasons and the remaining formal
requirements.

247
00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:03.800
This does not mean every late claim is automatically approved.

248
00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:08.970
Batch 1 covered basics, domestic travel, booking, claim
deadlines and some

249
00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:11.470
verified FAQs and amendments.

250
00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:15.990
For example, a Level 7 trainee checks entitlement and booking
before a flight,

251
00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:19.800
and the certificate and claim deadlines after the trip.

252
00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:24.350
Full Daily Allowance and road-rate tables, plus remaining
transfer, retirement

253
00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:28.290
and technical-resignation conditions, will come in later
batches; the complete

254
00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:30.390
course is not finished yet.

255
00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:33.590
Detailed examples and official source links are in the
companion guide.

256
00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:35.130
Thanks for watching!
